---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber off
    actor Steward
    participant Profile as Profile page<br/>(Proposed)
    participant Action as Server action<br/>updateOwnProfile<br/>(Proposed)
    participant Auth as Supabase Auth
    participant DB as Supabase<br/>PostgreSQL

    Note over Steward,DB: Covers US 1.0.2. No profile edit exists in the code. All steps are Proposed.

    Steward->>Profile: Open own profile and select Edit
    activate Profile
    Note right of Profile: The Edit control shows only on the<br/>profile of the signed-in user (AT1).
    Steward->>Profile: Change name, email, skills or focus areas
    Steward->>Profile: Select Save
    Profile->>Profile: Check that name and email are not empty (AT3)

    alt Name or email is empty
        Profile-->>Steward: Block save and highlight the empty field (AT3)
    else Fields are filled
        Profile->>Action: updateOwnProfile(fields)
        activate Action
        Action->>Auth: getUser() from the session cookie
        activate Auth
        Auth-->>Action: Signed-in user id or no user
        deactivate Auth
        Note right of Action: The action edits only the session user.<br/>A user id from the client is not trusted.

        alt No session
            Action-->>Profile: Refuse (401)
            Profile-->>Steward: Go to /login
        else Request names another user (AT1, AT2)
            Action-->>Profile: Refuse (403), no write
            Profile-->>Steward: Show "You can edit only your own profile"
        else Own profile
            Action->>Action: Check name and email again on server (AT3)
            alt Name or email not valid
                Action-->>Profile: Field errors (422)
                Profile-->>Steward: Highlight the fields with errors
            else Values are valid
                Action->>DB: Update profiles row of session user<br/>(proposed)
                activate DB
                alt Database error
                    DB-->>Action: Error
                    Action-->>Profile: Save failed (500)
                    Profile-->>Steward: Show error and keep the typed values
                else Update done
                    DB-->>Action: Saved profile
                    Action-->>Profile: Saved profile
                    Profile-->>Steward: Show new values, skills and focus areas (AT4, AT6)
                end
                deactivate DB
            end
        end
        deactivate Action
    end
    deactivate Profile

    Note over Steward,DB: Values are read from the database on each load. After sign out and sign in,<br/>the profile shows the saved values (AT5). If the email is also the sign-in email,<br/>a change must go through Supabase Auth (open question).
